nodecode-myeline is a rewrite of Sandbox-Group-LLC's Sandbox-Group-LLC/myeline-hermes:

  https://github.com/Sandbox-Group-LLC/myeline-hermes
  commit df6b3c81fb74261c6e7693f905ad9a5d1e73270f
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Sandbox Group LLC (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the whole repository at that commit: two manifests
and a skill. Its ritual is carried over word for word in the place the model
reads it — every memory is a single fact with its source attached; an AI can
only propose, and nothing goes live until a person approves it; search
approved memory before answering questions about the user's own or their
team's history, and say so when nothing approved matches rather than guess;
offer to remember once, only on a yes, one atomic sentence that stands alone
tomorrow; file the day's card at sign-off as facts learned, decisions made
and open loops; retiring a fact for good takes a written reason that stays in
the audit log; and passwords, API keys, and card and bank numbers are
refused at every setting. The four tools keep their names (cortex_query,
cortex_remember, cortex_daily_card, cortex_retract) and their argument
shapes, and approval stays a human act the model cannot perform.

What was rewritten, and how: the original is a remote MCP server — a cortex
at one host that Hermes reaches over OAuth, so one person's memory is shared
by every assistant connected to it. Here the store is one JSON file in the
folder the section names, written atomically under the folder's lock, and the
four tools are NLE:DEFINE-CELL registrations instead of an MCP server's tool
list. The review queue, the audit log and the receipts are the same idea on
this computer, and the person's side, which in the original is a web
workspace, is the /myeline command.

What was left out, and why: the remote cortex and its OAuth sign-in, because
a Nodecode cell talks to the machine it runs on and a local file needs no
account, no token and no network; one retraction applying to every connected
assistant at once, which follows from the shared server and is not a fact a
single machine can promise; team brains shared between accounts; the free
plan's 200-fact cap and billing — the ceiling is a setting here; and the
workspace page's swipe interface, which /myeline review, approve and reject
replace in the conversation. LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
